 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "theres water in the bottom of my frige under the salad draws, keeps comming back after i mop it up"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Water pooling under the salad drawers usually means the defrost water isn't draining away properly and is backing up into the fridge compartment. The most common cause is a blockage in the small drain hole at the bottom of the back wall inside the fridge. Please check if that drain hole is visible and whether it looks blocked by food debris or ice. If you can see it, try gently clearing it with warm water from a squeezy bottle or a turkey baster."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ah ok i had a look and theres a little groove at the bottom of the back wall with a hole in it, and its full of bits of lettuce and gunk. i poked it out with a cotton bud and poured some warm water down and it went straight down. is that it then?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, that is almost certainly it. Since the water drained away immediately after you cleared the gunk, the blockage was preventing normal defrost condensation from escaping and has now been fixed. To stop this happening again, try to keep food packets slightly back from the rear wall so they don't trap debris in the drain channel, and give it a quick check every few months. If you find water appearing again despite the drain being clear, let me know."
  }
 ],
